  "readme": [
    {
      "section": "dsh-maestro-mobile",
      "text": "Mobile adaptation for the DeepSeek Harness (DSH) Web UI. On touch-primary devices below 1024px it turns the sidebar into an overlay drawer, sheets the dialogs, and tunes the composer for phones; any mouse-driven window, at every width, is a complete no-op — a narrow desktop window or a scaled display never gets the mobile shell."
    },
    {
      "section": "What you get",
      "text": "| Capability | How it works |\n|---|---|\n| Sidebar → drawer | On touch-primary devices below 1024px the sidebar becomes a left overlay drawer (~80vw, `transform:none` when open); desktop is untouched at every width |\n| Dialogs → sheets | Settings, explorer, and preview become mobile-friendly bottom sheets with `env(safe-area-inset-*)` handling and notch avoidance |\n| Status-bar & safe areas | Status-bar / notch padding, light/dark `theme-color`, and `touch-action: manipulation` + `gesturestart` guard against double-tap zoom |\n| Composer stays clean | Permission capsule, model name, and switch menus use fixed-size pinning so they never squeeze or overlap on narrow screens |\n| Tablet friendly | 768–1023px centered, width-constrained sheets; phone and tablet geometries are verified separately |\n| Easy diagnostics | Append `?dsh-maestro-mobile-debug=1` for a floating bar with viewport / frame / floating-panel / JS-error state |"
    },
    {
      "section": "Requirements",
      "text": "- Node.js ≥ 22, pnpm ≥ 11\n- A running [DeepSeek Harness](https://github.com/deepseek-ai/deepseek-harness) `web` profile (`pnpm dsh web`), DSH `0.2.x` (verified on `0.2.2-alpha.2`)\n- Chromium 105+ for the `:has()` selectors"
    },
    {
      "section": "Requirements",
      "text": "Response compression is the host's job when it is enabled: with `webServer`\nconfigured `compression: gzip` (the deployed profile does this) the plugin leaves\nthe responses alone, because DSH's own middleware already serves brotli/gzip and\nwins the `writeHead` race. On a profile that keeps the host default\n(`compression: none`) the plugin installs its own transparent gzip/brotli patch."
    },
    {
      "section": "Install",
      "text": "```sh"
    },
    {
      "section": "from the registry",
      "text": "dsh plugin --profile web add @ddtcorex/dsh-maestro-mobile"
    },
    {
      "section": "local development (live link: edit + rebuild just works)",
      "text": "dsh plugin --profile web add link:/path/to/dsh-maestro-mobile\n```\n\n`lib/` is gitignored build output: `pnpm build` produces it locally, and `pnpm-workspace.yaml` carries the `allowBuilds.esbuild` entry a fresh install needs. Restart `dsh web` after installing or after any `pnpm build`."
    },
    {
      "section": "Manual `cordis.yml` row",
      "text": "If you are not using `dsh plugin`, add this row to your `cordis.yml`:\n\n```yaml\n- id: maestro-mobile\n  name: '@ddtcorex/dsh-maestro-mobile'\n```"
    },
    {
      "section": "Development",
      "text": "```sh\npnpm install        # install (pnpm@11.7.0, lockfile v9)\npnpm verify         # type-check host + client (tsc --noEmit)\npnpm test           # node --test tests/*.test.ts (full suite)\npnpm test:core      # node --test tests/reconciler-core.test.ts tests/composer-keyboard-touch.test.ts (fast subset)\n\n`pnpm build` is the required gate after any source change; `lib/` is gitignored build output, so a change is incomplete until the build refreshes it locally."
    },
    {
      "section": "Development",
      "text": "Optional CDP regression probe (requires a live DSH Web on `:3080`, PIN cookie; to probe the raw server instead, set `DSH_PROBE_URL=http://127.0.0.1:3082/?token=<launch-token>` as in `docs/upstream/upgrade-runbook.md` §2):\n\n```sh\nDSH_PROBE_SESSION_ID=<id> pnpm smoke:cdp\n```"
    },
    {
      "section": "Architecture",
      "text": "- Host / client split is load-bearing: `src/index.ts` owns the session-delete route (`POST /api/mobile-nav.session.delete`) plus the conditional response-compression patch; all browser behavior lives in `src/client/`.\n- The delete route authenticates through the host (`connection.requestRejection`) because the `/api` launch-token fence is a prefix route that an exact route shadows; it fails closed with `503 admission-unavailable` when the host publishes no connection service.\n- `src/client/index.tsx` injects `['slots','layout','locale','sessionLogDownload','sessions','workspaces']`, registers locale dictionaries, injects one `<style data-plugin>` tag, and registers three slots (`MobileNavToggle` in the session header, `MobileDrawerFooter` in the sidebar foot, `ShellOverlay` backdrop + FAB).\n- Shared full-tree reconciler: `src/client/core/reconciler-core.ts` (zero-import engine) + `phone-chrome.ts` (a single `MutationObserver` driving `installMobileEffect`).\n- Styles are concatenated `tokens → base → layout → sheet → explorer-sheet → composer → settings-sheet → misc` into one tag; mobile rules target `(max-width: 1023px) and (pointer: coarse)`."
    },
    {
      "section": "License",
